Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.27,0:00:03.69,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}Vigo's Intel
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.79,0:00:04.43,Main - Top,Licia,0,0,0,,I believe someone else was \Nbehind Vigo's operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.25,0:00:10.48,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,Maybe Borotz was directing \NVigo to undermine Canarre.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.48,0:00:14.98,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,Magic items of invisibility are rare. \NYou wouldn't just stumble upon one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.98,0:00:18.91,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,Maybe he arranged things \Nto put it in Vigo's hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.51,0:00:22.41,Default,Licia,0,0,0,,I'm also concerned about \Nsomething else he mentioned…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.82,0:00:24.89,Flashback,Vigo,0,0,0,,Speaking of, Borotz said something…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.89,0:00:27.79,Flashback,Vigo,0,0,0,,He said we couldn't let the kid live.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.79,0:00:31.42,Flashback,Vigo,0,0,0,,He was asking around about assassins, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.42,0:00:35.00,Default,Charlotte,0,0,0,,But why would he do that so openly?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.00,0:00:39.06,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,He probably doesn't care \Nif we find out about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.03,0:00:42.96,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,If you hole up in your mansion \Nfor fear of assassination,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.96,0:00:46.53,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,you won't be able to recruit anyone \Nelse, and Canarre will stagnate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.53,0:00:49.84,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,If you never find out and continue hiring,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.84,0:00:53.07,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,they can just send their \Nassassin to kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.45,0:00:56.88,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,Your power is only useful if \Nyou meet someone face-to-face.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.88,0:00:59.58,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,His plan seems to use that against you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.58,0:01:04.00,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,True. I can't use my power \Nuntil I meet someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.00,0:01:08.76,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,But I can likely identify \Nthe assassin once I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.76,0:01:11.96,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,If he means to test my eye, \NI'll accept his challenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.38,0:01:16.09,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Nevertheless, Lord Ars, \Nyou must be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.51,0:01:20.41,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Anyone you encounter might be an assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.39,0:01:24.29,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Are we clear on the plan? See it done, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.02,0:02:57.78,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\shad0\bord1\blur1\fnArial Black\c&HD6D1D2&\pos(320,292)\3c&H161B1A&}One Week Later
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.87,0:02:57.78,Main - Top,Ars,0,0,0,,Isn't this too many people?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.78,0:03:01.16,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(520,480)\fs14\an3\shad1\bord1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HCACAC9&\3c&H302F2E&\4c&H302F2E&\pos(605.83,316.351)}Episode 33   {\fs16}Long-Standing Feelings
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.78,0:03:00.61,Main - Top,Ars,0,0,0,,This is more than double\N the turnout from last time!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.61,0:03:03.49,Main - Top,Rietz,0,0,0,,That's thanks to Canarre's\N success in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.49,0:03:06.83,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Our victory spells better pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.83,0:03:09.76,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Military positions in Castle \NCanarre are quite sought after.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.76,0:03:13.25,Default,Charlotte,0,0,0,,And thanks to Musia, we've \Nhad more female recruits, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.73,0:03:16.12,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,We're even getting applicants \Nfrom other provinces,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.12,0:03:18.26,Default,Rosell,0,0,0,,which expands the recruiting pool!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.26,0:03:21.58,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,I see. It's all connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.58,0:03:25.36,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,Getting excellent talent \Nlets us win campaigns,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.36,0:03:27.77,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,and that lets us recruit even \Nmore excellent talent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.64,0:03:32.27,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,I can't refuse to meet people \Nfor fear of assassins.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.81,0:03:36.77,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,For Canarre's sake as well, I have \Nto keep this momentum going!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.77,0:03:40.03,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}A New Recruit
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.68,0:03:40.03,Main - Top,Rietz,0,0,0,,Next applicant, if you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.91,0:03:59.92,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\shad0\fnArial\blur2\bord3\fs18\b1\3c&HC0DA59&\4c&HCFDB77&\c&HF1EBBA&\pos(320,280)}Enan Rueges   21   Female
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.24,0:03:52.83,Main - Top + Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,I've seen over fifty people today, \Nand she's got the best Ingenuity by far!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.83,0:03:54.94,Main - Top + Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,Her affinity as a smith is S-rank, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.94,0:03:57.68,Main - Top + Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,That's the best I've seen since Shin!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.68,0:04:01.48,Main - Top + Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,Maybe she could help him\N develop his airship!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.92,0:04:04.43,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\bord1\fnArial Black\fs16\an8\c&H5398E3&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&H73E6FB&\pos(320,255)}Born in 191 of the Imperial Calendar in Missian. \NParents deceased, two older brothers…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.01,0:04:04.43,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,Nothing suspicious in her history.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.82,0:04:08.16,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,And her physical stats \Nseem low for an assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.16,0:04:10.93,Main - Italics,Ars,0,0,0,,What a truly lucky find!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.72,0:04:15.07,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I am Ars Louvent,\N headman of Canarre District.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.07,0:04:17.44,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Would you mind if I asked your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.57,0:04:28.83,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs14\shad0\bord1.2\pos(320,295)\c&HB7B7B7&\3c&H323234&\b1}As I cannot speak, would it be acceptable for me to communicate in writing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.47,0:04:32.54,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.11,0:04:41.11,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Enan Rueges, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.11,0:04:43.34,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,And you hail from Coumeire?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.90,0:04:46.09,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,You have beautiful penmanship.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.72,0:04:50.36,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Why are you applying?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.51,0:04:56.12,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,You were hoping to be useful?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.12,0:04:57.98,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Yes, I see…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.40,0:05:02.11,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Well, I'd like to hire you at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.49,0:05:05.73,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Here you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.23,0:05:25.81,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,She seemed almost conflicted.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.81,0:05:27.03,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,Are you sure about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.03,0:05:30.04,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Yes. I didn't see anything to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.04,0:05:32.06,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I don't think she's an assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.06,0:05:33.89,Default,Charlotte,0,0,0,,Hang on a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.89,0:05:37.39,Default,Charlotte,0,0,0,,My woman's intuition tells \Nme she's up to something!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.87,0:05:45.01,Default,Licia,0,0,0,,Yes, it's unusual for someone common-born \Nto have such lovely penmanship.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.01,0:05:48.71,Default,Licia,0,0,0,,Lord Ars, I would advise looking into her.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.71,0:05:51.03,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,I agree with the two of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.03,0:05:54.15,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Pham! Why makes you say so?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.15,0:05:57.41,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,I don't know what that woman's after,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.41,0:06:00.54,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,but she's been examining the \Ncastle and writing things down.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.54,0:06:02.44,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I had no idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.44,0:06:03.86,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.86,0:06:06.92,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Pham, could I ask you to investigate Enan?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.22,0:06:08.38,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,No problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.46,0:06:23.32,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.60,0:06:26.32,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,You got Lord Ars to hire you, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.13,0:06:33.33,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Enan is a maid?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.60,0:06:38.58,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Yeah. I followed her to a \Nmerchant's residence in Coumeire.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.26,0:06:42.08,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Looks like she's a live-in apprentice there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.48,0:06:44.70,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Why would she come to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.70,0:06:47.21,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Surely a merchant's house pays well…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.68,0:06:50.55,Main - Top,Pham,0,0,0,,No worries. I'll find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.30,0:06:53.22,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}Maid Infiltration
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.95,0:06:57.90,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Here you are, Madam!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.90,0:06:59.48,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Fresh out of the oven!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.48,0:07:01.55,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Oh, spectacular!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.55,0:07:02.98,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,They all look delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.31,0:07:05.86,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,You're so sweet and charming, Lynn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.86,0:07:07.99,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,I'm so glad I hired you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.43,0:07:09.99,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,By comparison…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.40,0:07:13.12,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,look at that moody little wretch.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.48,0:07:15.70,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Come, let us enjoy these together.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.70,0:07:16.61,Default,Maids,0,0,0,,Yes, Madam!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.12,0:07:21.62,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Say, doesn't the madam seem \Nawfully hard on Enan to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.62,0:07:23.38,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She really is!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.38,0:07:25.80,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She's nice to everyone else,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.80,0:07:29.01,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,but she's cruel to Enan for some reason!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.40,0:07:32.40,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She's the most competent \Nmaid in the household, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.40,0:07:36.89,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She's the only one who's been \Nhere since the previous madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.37,0:07:40.64,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Gosh, I gotta say,\N this sure is a big house!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.64,0:07:41.88,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,Isn't it just?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.88,0:07:45.16,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,They're the most prominent \Nmerchant family in Coumeire!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.16,0:07:49.20,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,Though the master's almost never here, \Nas he travels around the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.20,0:07:51.68,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,I hear the previous madam\Nwas a wonderful person, too,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.68,0:07:53.60,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,but she passed from some kind of illness,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.60,0:07:57.28,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,and he remarried with the current madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.92,0:08:01.07,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Why doesn't Enan ever speak?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.07,0:08:01.91,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Is she sick?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.91,0:08:03.44,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,No idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.44,0:08:06.92,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,But I hear she could speak \Nunder the previous madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.92,0:08:09.56,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Has she been up to anything recently?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.56,0:08:12.74,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Like, say, paying a visit \Nto Seitz Province?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.74,0:08:15.17,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,I've never heard anything like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.17,0:08:19.62,Main - Top,Maid A,0,0,0,,She was born here in Coumeire, \Nand as far as I know, she's never left.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.64,0:08:19.62,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,Enan Rueges…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.62,0:08:21.99,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,There's too much I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.99,0:08:24.31,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,I'll have to make direct contact.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.66,0:08:26.56,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.56,0:08:29.07,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,You're making Enan do all of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.37,0:08:32.32,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,The duchess is visiting in two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.32,0:08:34.57,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,We need to tidy things up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.96,0:08:37.36,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,But it's already dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.36,0:08:39.24,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,At least let us help her—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.24,0:08:43.01,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Oh, I think very highly \Nof Enan's abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.01,0:08:44.96,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,You have the skills to get it done, yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.96,0:08:49.36,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,None of you help her, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.36,0:08:52.40,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Come, let's get inside before it rains.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.22,0:09:09.00,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,This must be hard by yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.00,0:09:10.08,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Let me lend a hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.81,0:09:27.12,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,All done!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.12,0:09:29.16,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Ah, I'm bushed!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.16,0:09:33.71,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Gosh, what a rotten thing \Nthe madam made you do!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.29,0:09:36.56,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,"Thanks," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.56,0:09:38.98,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Hey, it's no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.98,0:09:42.87,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,I can't wait to see the shock \Non the madam's face!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.31,0:09:46.94,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs14\shad0\bord1.2\pos(320,295)\c&HB7B7B7&\3c&H323234&\b1}I'd like to frame her expression and place it in the entrance hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.91,0:09:50.19,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,I'd love that, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.19,0:09:53.65,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,But I bet it would drive visitors away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.65,0:09:56.49,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs14\shad0\bord1.2\pos(320,295)\c&HB7B7B7&\3c&H323234&\b1}The plaque below would read, "Madam in a Moment of Shock."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.44,0:10:02.48,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,I thought she was moody, \Nbut that's not her true self.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.48,0:10:05.17,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,She did a fantastic job \Ntending the garden, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.17,0:10:08.55,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,Her abilities live up to Ars's estimation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.15,0:10:12.04,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,I suppose I should stick around and watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.55,0:10:44.96,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,What could she be up to at this hour?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.75,0:10:49.72,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,Where the hell is she going?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.83,0:10:55.11,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,She disappeared?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.55,0:11:04.01,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}Enan's Secret
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.55,0:11:04.01,Main - Top + Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,This is where Enan disappeared last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.01,0:11:05.70,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,How did she do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.98,0:11:39.74,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Looks like Ars was right about her gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.66,0:11:44.68,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Is this information about poisons?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.99,0:11:47.96,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Is Enan trying to poison Ars?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.19,0:11:55.44,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,A diary?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.18,0:11:59.80,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,July 8th. In order to practice my writing,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.80,0:12:02.04,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I'm going to start keeping a diary.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.20,0:12:05.70,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(480,400)\fs18\shad1\bord1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HC8CCC9&\3c&H232C28&\4c&H232C28&\pos(325,290)}Enan, Age 15
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.20,0:12:05.70,Flashback - Top,Enan,0,0,0,,Look, Madam! I finished it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.70,0:12:09.87,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,Why, Enan! That's much \Nbetter than what I can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.87,0:12:12.88,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,You can really can do \Nanything once you're taught.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.88,0:12:15.21,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,You pick things up so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.70,0:12:18.21,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I came to the estate \Nfor an apprenticeship,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.21,0:12:20.75,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,and the madam taught me many things.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.75,0:12:24.16,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,Listen, don't tell the master \Nabout this room, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.16,0:12:27.10,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Of course! It's our little secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.38,0:12:28.73,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,Listen, Enan…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.26,0:12:32.48,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,I don't think you should \Nstay with us forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.48,0:12:34.98,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,I'll free you from your \Napprenticeship eventually, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.98,0:12:39.05,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,What? But why? Because \NI'm not good at housework?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.05,0:12:43.20,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,No, but a maid's work is \Na waste of your talents.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.20,0:12:46.78,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,You should study, learn a trade, \Nand strike out on your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.78,0:12:49.62,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,You'll make a much better living that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.02,0:12:52.95,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,In fact, because you're \Nso good with your hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.95,0:12:54.50,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,how about becoming an artisan?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.02,0:12:58.00,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,I just know you'd do it wonderfully!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.29,0:13:05.47,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Oh, Madam! \NI'd rather stay with you forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.81,0:13:08.23,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,Oh, you silly thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.23,0:13:09.92,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,I'm tickled, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.92,0:13:11.97,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,By the way, can you write?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.45,0:13:13.52,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,No…
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.52,0:13:16.06,Flashback,Former Madam,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll teach you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.23,0:13:21.48,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,Soon after, the madam passed \Nfrom an unknown illness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.88,0:13:28.80,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Enan's penmanship is so good because \Nthe previous madam taught her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.52,0:13:40.86,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Hey, it's time for lunch. Let's eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.55,0:13:50.10,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,"I have to go shopping on Madam's behalf."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.10,0:13:51.84,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Oh, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.02,0:13:57.04,Main - Top,Maids,0,0,0,,No, that's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.04,0:14:00.05,Main - Top,Maids,0,0,0,,I think it would look great on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.22,0:14:01.27,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Hey, where did Enan go \Non her shopping errand?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.27,0:14:04.28,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,What? No one's meant to go shopping today.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.67,0:14:08.60,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She disappears from time to time at noon.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.60,0:14:10.28,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.28,0:14:13.03,Main - Top,Maid C,0,0,0,,I wonder what she's up to…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.82,0:14:13.03,Main - Italics,Pham,0,0,0,,Guess I'll follow her next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.03,0:14:15.29,Default,Bodyguard A,0,0,0,,Hey, we're outta booze.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.52,0:14:19.04,Default,Bodyguard A,0,0,0,,Wow, aren't you a cutie?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.39,0:14:21.40,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,Hold it. Leave her alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.40,0:14:23.04,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,She's new.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.40,0:14:23.04,Main - Top,Bodyguards,0,0,0,,This one's nice, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.04,0:14:24.80,Main - Top,Bodyguards,0,0,0,,She's got it all!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.80,0:14:26.27,Main - Top,Bodyguards,0,0,0,,Let's take her!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.41,0:14:27.05,Default,Maid A,0,0,0,,Honestly, you went through all that already?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.05,0:14:30.30,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,You okay, Lynn? I'm sure that was scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.61,0:14:33.24,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Who were those rude men?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.24,0:14:36.20,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,Bodyguards the madam hired.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.20,0:14:38.18,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,They live and work in the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.70,0:14:41.12,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,It's really hard to get a read on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.12,0:14:44.39,Default,Maid B,0,0,0,,All they do is drink and gamble all day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.39,0:14:47.38,Default,Maid C,0,0,0,,Why in the world did she even hire them?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.31,0:14:57.33,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Any tidings from Castle Canarre yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.33,0:15:00.83,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}The Truth
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.62,0:15:00.83,Main - Top,Madam,0,0,0,,I hope it'll happen soon…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.33,0:15:05.59,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Looks like you still can't \Nuse that throat we crushed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.18,0:15:13.01,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,After my madam passed away \Nfrom a sudden disease,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.01,0:15:15.34,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,a new madam came along.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.35,0:15:19.23,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,She said she was a friend of my old madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.23,0:15:21.52,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,She saw that I was depressed\Nand tried to cheer me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.52,0:15:23.14,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,She seemed like such a kind woman…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.73,0:15:25.23,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,until that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.24,0:15:28.99,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Move her grave? Now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.28,0:15:34.42,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,The master did say he'd like to move it \Nto a plot with a nicer view, but…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.42,0:15:37.61,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we wait for his return?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.61,0:15:40.85,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,I don't want to trouble\N the master with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.85,0:15:43.63,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,But it's dangerous, \Nso you don't need to help.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.10,0:15:51.34,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,I can't let the madam and her men \Nhandle it alone in this storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.34,0:15:53.22,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,I'll lend a hand and—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.34,0:15:57.72,Flashback,Bodyguard A,0,0,0,,That poison was a lousy idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.07,0:16:03.72,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Tea brewed from deo herbs\N was the best way to kill her.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.72,0:16:07.23,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Nobody even suspected she was poisoned!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.23,0:16:09.59,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Now, clean this up quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.59,0:16:13.24,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,We can't have anyone seeing the way \Nthe poison changed the bones' color.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.68,0:16:14.74,Flashback - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.42,0:16:16.74,Flashback - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,Madam was…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.75,0:16:22.41,Flashback - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,killed?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.41,0:16:23.92,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,What's this? Enan?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.92,0:16:26.45,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Why? Why did you kill her?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.45,0:16:28.29,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,Weren't you friends?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.73,0:16:31.56,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,She was in my way, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.56,0:16:33.80,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Marrying a merchant\N is guaranteed security.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.15,0:16:35.92,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,That's the only reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.86,0:16:38.56,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,How dare you…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.03,0:16:40.72,Flashback,Enan,0,0,0,,I won't let this stand!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.72,0:16:43.76,Flashback,Bodyguard B,0,0,0,,What do we do with her? Kill her?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.76,0:16:47.35,Flashback,Bodyguard A,0,0,0,,Dumbass. Two deaths in a row \Nwould look suspicious as hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.35,0:16:52.07,Flashback,Bodyguard C,0,0,0,,And the master likes her, so we \Ncan't dismiss her without a reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.62,0:16:54.45,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Let's see, then…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.82,0:16:57.20,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,Torture her just enough that
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.61,0:16:59.47,Flashback,Madam,0,0,0,,she won't feel like talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.86,0:17:08.08,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,They crushed my throat, \Nleaving me unable to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.74,0:17:11.59,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,They disposed of the evidence, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.92,0:17:14.72,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,My madam's soul will never \Nbe at peace like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.82,0:17:21.26,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I'm going to bring this villainy to light!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.98,0:17:26.76,Default,Bodyguard C,0,0,0,,So, what do we do next?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.76,0:17:30.71,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,We'll use her to sell our \Ngoods to Castle Canarre.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.71,0:17:33.20,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,The headman is said to pay well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.20,0:17:35.58,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,We can get even richer!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.58,0:17:37.11,Default,Bodyguard B,0,0,0,,That's our madam!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.87,0:17:42.38,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,"I will no longer follow your orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.38,0:17:45.28,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,I will report your crimes to Lord Ars.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.28,0:17:47.62,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Before I do, you should turn yourself in."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.83,0:17:52.46,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Did you forget what happens\Nif you oppose me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.09,0:17:58.64,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.64,0:18:01.85,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,So you killed the merchant's \Nprevious wife, did you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.85,0:18:03.86,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,You're that maid…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.86,0:18:05.10,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,No, who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.10,0:18:07.15,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,This must've been hard on you, Enan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.15,0:18:09.97,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,You'll be all right now.\N Leave the rest to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.86,0:18:13.86,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Maybe I'll crush your throat, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.32,0:18:16.35,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,You should really think before you act.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.35,0:18:17.69,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,Men!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.69,0:18:18.40,Default,Bodyguard A/B,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.64,0:18:30.17,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,You asked who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.17,0:18:31.95,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,My name is Pham.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.95,0:18:35.00,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,I'm a retainer of Canarre's \Nheadman, Ars Louvent,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.00,0:18:37.92,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,and the leader of the Shadow Company.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.92,0:18:39.93,Default,Bodyguard C,0,0,0,,Y-You're from Canarre?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.93,0:18:42.80,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,So what? You have no proof—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.62,0:18:46.72,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,The burnt remains of the tools \Nyou used to dig up the grave,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.72,0:18:48.86,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,testimony from the merchant\Nwho sold you the poison,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.86,0:18:53.82,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,and an analysis of the poison extracted \Nfrom the previous madam's bones.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.08,0:18:55.57,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Right, Enan?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.07,0:19:00.49,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,430)\shad1\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs18\c&HC6CCCE&\3c&H161B1A&\pos(175,307)}Enan Rueges
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.07,0:18:59.52,Main - Top,Madam,0,0,0,,This is all a setup!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.52,0:19:02.41,Main - Top,Madam,0,0,0,,We threw all her bones into the river!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.06,0:19:08.42,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,This is a bone from my late madam.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.46,0:19:19.98,Flashback - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,Madam…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.46,0:19:24.97,Default,Madam,0,0,0,,No! I thought it was flawless!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.22,0:19:30.30,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I don't care that you took my voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.84,0:19:31.62,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,But…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.56,0:19:36.84,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I'll never forgive you for \Nkilling my beloved madam!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.24,0:19:41.74,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I can't believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.74,0:19:44.08,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,The merchant's second wife was arrested.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.08,0:19:49.37,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,She and her lackeys will be in prison \Nfor a long time for murder and battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.69,0:19:53.50,Default,Rietz,0,0,0,,So that's why Enan \Nwas acting so strangely.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.02,0:19:58.80,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,As your lord, I take full responsibility \Nfor failing to realize this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.80,0:20:02.84,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,If you ever need anything, \Nno matter how small, please ask me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.84,0:20:07.51,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I'm here to protect the good \Npeople of Canarre, like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.02,0:20:11.10,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,But it really is a shame!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.10,0:20:14.81,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,You didn't actually come \Nhere to work for me…
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.81,0:20:17.27,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Please take care heading home.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.27,0:20:19.03,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,I wish you all the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.05,0:20:22.78,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,You cool with that, Enan?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.13,0:20:25.96,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Heading back to work as a maid again?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.96,0:20:27.75,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,This is a good place.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.75,0:20:30.95,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,You can put your talents to \Ntheir best possible use here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.95,0:20:33.92,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Isn't that what your old \Nmadam would have wanted?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.80,0:20:43.27,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,Would working together let \Nus become better friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.15,0:20:46.96,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'll say.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.81,0:20:50.64,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Ars! Enan wants to work here!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.64,0:20:52.31,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,What? You're sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.88,0:20:56.68,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I look forward to working with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.31,0:21:00.32,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\shad0\bord1\blur1\fnArial Black\c&HD6D1D2&\pos(320,292)\3c&H161B1A&}Louvent Estate, Lamberg
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.70,0:21:00.32,Main - Top,Mireille,0,0,0,,He's in that shed there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.59,0:21:02.43,Default,Mireille,0,0,0,,Well, good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.28,0:21:08.28,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Wait, don't go down yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.75,0:21:11.01,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Not again!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.90,0:21:18.96,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Pretty awesome airship, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.96,0:21:22.59,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Once it starts flying, \Nit'll use half the magistones—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.59,0:21:25.14,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Huh? "The curve of the wood is wrong"?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.14,0:21:26.35,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,How so?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.21,0:21:32.53,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,The tips of the wings need to be sharper, \Nor it'll cause wind resistance.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.53,0:21:35.08,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Yeah, but getting the curve \Nright is the hard part!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.08,0:21:37.74,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,The wood's light, but it's hard to shape…
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.22,0:21:39.86,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,I think I can handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.86,0:21:40.85,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,You mean it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.85,0:21:44.32,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,You're awesome! You wanna help me work?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.32,0:21:46.11,Main - Italics,Enan,0,0,0,,That's why I was asked to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.11,0:21:49.99,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Man, I was needing more hands! \NYou'll be a huge help!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.49,0:21:55.00,Default,Shin,0,0,0,,Enan, is it? Lookin' forward \Nto workin' with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.73,0:23:28.80,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Isn't it nice to have a new friend, Pham?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.80,0:23:29.53,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.53,0:23:32.12,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,By the way, did you have friends before?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.12,0:23:35.58,Default,Pham,0,0,0,,Ars, I'm requesting ten times \Nthe usual amount for this job.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.58,0:23:37.52,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,P-Please, forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.52,0:23:40.02,Default,Ars,0,0,0,,Next time: "Two Exceptional Talents."
